---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '18 February 2025';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for the bank statement to Excel converter, including the accuracy disclaimer, the limits of the tool, and the absence of any warranty."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="page prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="small muted">Last updated {updated}.</p>

      <div class="note note--warn">
        <strong>Read this part.</strong> This tool converts the contents of a PDF or OFX file into a spreadsheet. It does
        not audit your bank, verify your bank's arithmetic, or check that a statement is correct or complete. Conversion
        can contain errors. Always check the output against your original statement before you file, reconcile, report or
        lend against it.
      </div>

      <h2>1. What this service is</h2>
      <p>
        This site provides a browser-based file conversion tool. The conversion runs on your device. We do not receive,
        store or process your files, and we provide no server-side conversion service under these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including
        but not limited to fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the
        conversion will be complete, correct, uninterrupted, or suitable for any particular accounting, tax, audit or
        lending purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Your responsibility to verify</h2>
      <p>
        You are solely responsible for verifying any output before relying on it. The tool provides aids for this — a
        running-balance reconciliation count, per-row flags, and a Raw sheet containing the source text line behind each
        row — but these are aids, not guarantees, and they can be defeated by unusual statement layouts.
      </p>
      <p>
        Check at minimum: the number of rows, the total of the amounts, and the final balance against the closing balance
        printed on your statement.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Not financial, legal, tax or accounting advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site constitutes financial, legal, tax or accounting advice. The tool performs a mechanical
        conversion of a document you supply. Consult a qualified professional for advice about your accounts, taxes or
        financial position.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to use this service:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>to process documents you are not authorised to handle;</li>
        <li>to attempt to disrupt, overload or reverse-engineer the site;</li>
        <li>to scrape or republish its content as your own; or</li>
        <li>in any way that breaks applicable law, including data protection and financial regulation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or
        punitive damages, or for any loss of profits, revenue, data, or goodwill, arising out of or in connection with
        your use of the service — including any loss arising from an inaccurate conversion, a missed transaction, or a
        decision made on the basis of a converted file. Where liability cannot be excluded, it is limited to the greater
        of the amount you paid us (which, for the free tool, is zero) or the minimum permitted by law.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Third-party names and links</h2>
      <p>
        Bank names, Intuit QuickBooks, Xero and other product names are the trademarks of their respective owners. They
        appear on this site only to describe file formats and statement layouts. This site is not affiliated with,
        endorsed by or sponsored by any of them. Links to third-party sites, including affiliate links, are provided for
        convenience; we are not responsible for their content or practices.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The site's own text, design and code are ours. The documents you convert remain entirely yours — we never receive
        a copy, so no licence over them is granted or needed.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may change, suspend or discontinue any part of the service at any time, including limits on file size or page
        count. We may update these terms; the date at the top of this page will change when we do, and continued use after
        a change means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
